cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this convention, please cite it as below."
title: "rimi. — Open Convention for Conversational Reliability of LLMs"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Hiram"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-17"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22814989"
license: CC0-1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rimi-ai/rimi.convention"
url: "https://github.com/rimi-ai/rimi.convention"
abstract: >-
  An open, collaborative and testable convention that sets what a large
  language model does when it would otherwise guess, smooth over or invent:
  ambiguous answers, conflicting sources, missing data, and resource use.
  Conformance levels A, AA, AAA with a separate frugality indicator S1, S2, S3.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - conversational AI
  - reliability
  - hallucination
  - responsible AI
  - frugal AI
  - convention
  - consensus
